data.content:
Here's the output:

```json
{
  "Name": "Alice",
  "Age": 30
}
```

The key piece is `JsonNamingPolicy.PascalCase` — a built-in policy available since .NET 9. Since your record's constructor parameters are lowercase (`name`, `age`), the generated backing properties are also lowercase. `PascalCase` policy converts them to `Name` and `Age` in the serialized JSON.

The full program is at `PersonJson/Program.cs`:

```csharp
using System.Text.Json;

var person = new Person("Alice", 30);

var options = new JsonSerializerOptions
{
    PropertyNamingPolicy = JsonNamingPolicy.PascalCase,
    WriteIndented = true
};

string json = JsonSerializer.Serialize(person, options);
Console.WriteLine(json);

public record Person(string name, int age);
```
